{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1559951-could-the-vaulderie-cure-the-beckoning","id":1559951,"title":"Could the Vaulderie Cure the Beckoning?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-05-14T00:40:55-07:00","id":1559951,"title":"Could the Vaulderie Cure the Beckoning?","content":"Just had an epiphany about this situation.<br /> <br /> We know that the Beckoning is apparently being caused by the Antedeluvians putting out the call to arms for their more powerful clanmates. But the Vaulderie is supposed to sever all existing blood bonds and establish new ones with your collective pack.<br /> <br /> So, theoretically speaking, shouldn't the Sabbat be immune to the Beckoning's effects?<br /> <br /> I mean, the ritual was originally created specifically to shatter whatever control the elders had over their childer.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And if so, then anybody else who undergoes the Vaulderie should likewise be freed of the Beckoning's compulsion.<br /> <br /> It's a shame the Camarilla and the Anarchs are focused on killing the Sabbat on sight, instead of trying to work out some kind of truce.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-14T01:00:32-07:00","id":1559952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1559951-could-the-vaulderie-cure-the-beckoning#post1559951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We know that the Beckoning is apparently being caused by the Antedeluvians putting out the call to arms for their more powerful clanmates. But the Vaulderie is supposed to sever all existing blood bonds and establish new ones with your collective pack.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think a good test of this logic would be whether the Sabbat Ravnos were less effected by the Week of Nightmares? (I don't think it's mentioned, but I'm actually not sure).<br /> <br /> Also, the vaulderie not being nearly as potent as the Sabbat think wouldn't be that big a twist. The Sabbat have since their original creation been heavily implied to be a lot less successful than they think they are. They <i>think</i> they're free, but they're not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And if so, then anybody else who undergoes the Vaulderie should likewise be freed of the Beckoning's compulsion. </div> </div> </div>I don't understand your phrasing there. Like, we know it's not effective, it's a big part of the plot that the Sabbat aren't immune.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's a shame the Camarilla and the Anarchs are focused on killing the Sabbat on sight, instead of trying to work out some kind of truce. </div> </div> </div>That's not really the Camarilla and Anarchs' fault.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-14T01:07:11-07:00","id":1559953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1559951-could-the-vaulderie-cure-the-beckoning?p=1559952#post1559952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, the vaulderie not being nearly as potent as the Sabbat think wouldn't be that big a twist. The Sabbat have since their original creation been heavily implied to be a lot less successful than they think they are. They <i>think</i> they're free, but they're not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wasn't the Vaulderie co-developed by Kupala?<br /> <br /> If an earthbound demon can't get it right, then you're probably completely screwed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-14T08:57:26-07:00","id":1559958,"title":"","content":"The roots of the <b>Vaulderie </b>are in an ancient Koldunic ritual, <b>Kupala's Night</b><br /> It is actually detailed, so I will not bore you with the details but one of the key point is: &quot;The land and the ruler are one, and so the Transylvanian Tzimisce show their reverence for the land by sharing their blood with each other and the earth. With the assistance of mystics, participants enact an ancient rite involving the sharing of blood, A silver cup containing the vitae of all in the ceremony is passed around to be consumed and the last few drops are poured on the ground. &quot;<br /> <br /> Now there is a little confusion, or rather the things start to blend into each other<br /> <b>Kupala's Sacred Fire-Flower</b> (or Kupala's heart) was blood-red bloom, and a key ingredient of the ritual that used Lambach's potent blood as a catalyst that made possible to the Tzimisce koldun to break the Blood Bond with their elders<br /> As legend goes, Kupala created it and with it, sorcerers may bind or release demons.<br /> However... its roots sprouted from the depths of Yorak's domain and it was in fact a portion of the Eldest newest form \u2013 a precursor to the horror dwelling in the sewers of New York<br /> The whole point, in theory, was to shatter any former alliances shared by the Eldest and its progenies and and to impart its seeds into a new generation of Tzimisce, binding them to it alone - and as a neat little side effect, &quot;infecting&quot; the entire Sabbat<br /> <br /> Depending of the edition and from what angle you look it, it was probably the case and Kupala was just a spectator from the sidelines<br /> \u200b<br /> Anyhow, we don't 100% sure what the hell the Becoing actually was/is?<br /> A mysterious compulsion (starting around the 2010s) that draws elders (generally 9th Generation and lower, with stronger blood feeling it more) toward the Middle East and other ancient civilization cradles but it isn't explicitly framed as a standard blood bond from one's sire or clan Antediluvian.<br /> The Hecata seems to be &quot;immune&quot; to the Becoing, but they are a weird case anyway, because while you can trace back even the Samedi to the Cappadocians (or not, really depends on what you want; they are either a Drowned Legacy or Baron Samedi was either a bona fide Dath God that took a joyride in a corpse, not unlike how Azaneal, a Second Generation became a disembodied demonic spectre to a Qlippoth realm and used the husk of a Baali to walk the earth again, or the Child of eaither Lazarus or Troglodytia, the Queen Mother...) the Nagaraja are closest to the Followers of Set, since they used Setite vitae to their ritual and the Pisanob are again a bit murky what the hell are...<br /> So... eh?\u200b<br /> It's widely suspected to be tied to the Antediluvians or powerful Methuselahs calling their descendants - but no real evidance of that to be honest, it is just our best guess that may or may not true and diablerie, or consuming potent vitae can sometimes <i>temporarily</i> stave it off.<br /> Sometimes. \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> Now what we do know?<br /> Sabbat elders and ancillae <i>do</i> hear and follow the Beckoning en masse. The Sabbat as a sect has plunged into the Gehenna War because of it.<br /> So logically, if the Vaulderie reliably broke the effect, this wouldn't be happening on the observed scale.<br /> <br /> Lets be real here, the Sabbat's &quot;freedom&quot; via Vaulderie has always been more ideological and practical than absolute\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> The Sabbat aren't immune to the Beconing<br /> <br /> Should be?<br /> I don't really think so<br /> The Beckoning is more like a deep, psychic/mystical summons tied to the Blood itself and ancient powers awakening and while the Vaulderie targets personal/regnant bonds effectively, it doesn't seem to sever this broader call.<br /> Nor it protected the Sabbat Ravnos from the effects of the Week of Nightmares; Sabbat Ravnos suffered devastating losses but actually survived at higher rates than their Camarilla counterparts that is true but because the Ravnos were compelled to diablerize <i>each other </i>when Zapathasura got nuked (or left reality, dealers choice, fun fact, following the events of Reckoning of New York it is basically a fact, Blood of Zapathasura, the thick, sentient ropes of his vitae... has remained sentient since 1999)<br /> Because of the Sabbat's chaotic structure and nomadic pack tactics, many of their Ravnos were scattered and isolated, making them less likely to succumb to the localized, clan-wide cannibalistic frenzy and when they spiraled out of controll, their packmates staked them<br /> But everythig else also effected them, the power boost, the visions, everything<br /> <br /> So no, I would say nor it would be a &quot;cure&quot; nor helped the Sabbat<br /> Or should helped them, because the \u200bVaulderie was always something else\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-15T14:56:22-07:00","id":1559993,"title":"","content":"The mere fact that monomancy is so common strongly suggests that the Vaulderie has always been mostly propaganda. My headcanon has long been that the Vaulderie is basically like smoking a peace-pipe. It smooths over minor disagreements, but barely slows down the growth of hatred between two vampires who have legitimate cause to despise each other. The idea that it is this massively powerful thing that makes the Sabbat utterly unified and invincible is just what they tell the Camarilla.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-15T21:17:48-07:00","id":1560005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1559951-could-the-vaulderie-cure-the-beckoning?p=1559958#post1559958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">snip\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, well, if the Vaulderie doesn't break the connection, what about... urgh... the Panders ritual?<br /> <br /> The one that turns you into a Caitiff?<br /> <br /> Can't be compelled by the antedeluvians, if you have no antedeluvian! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-15T21:21:01-07:00","id":1560006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1559951-could-the-vaulderie-cure-the-beckoning?p=1559993#post1559993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The mere fact that monomancy is so common strongly suggests that the Vaulderie has always been mostly propaganda. My headcanon has long been that the Vaulderie is basically like smoking a peace-pipe. It smooths over minor disagreements, but barely slows down the growth of hatred between two vampires who have legitimate cause to despise each other. The idea that it is this massively powerful thing that makes the Sabbat utterly unified and invincible is just what they tell the Camarilla.</div> </div> </div> </div>From my understanding, the Sabbat don't hate the idea of elders being in charge. They hate the idea of incompetent elders being in charge.<br /> <br /> Monomancy exists to prove to the pack that you're not some push over. That you can actually defend your position from those who seek to usurp it.<br /> <br /> They don't tolerate weak, cowardly elders, who surround themselves with disposable meat shields while they flee to their reinforced panic rooms when shit hits the fan.<br /> <br /> Besides, part of the Gehenna prophecy talks about how <i>&quot;a black hand shall rise and choke out all who oppose it.&quot;</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-16T00:27:42-07:00","id":1560012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1559951-could-the-vaulderie-cure-the-beckoning?p=1560005#post1560005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, well, if the Vaulderie doesn't break the connection, what about... urgh... the Panders ritual?<br /> <br /> The one that turns you into a Caitiff?<br /> <br /> Can't be compelled by the antedeluvians, if you have no antedeluvian! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes<br /> And no<br /> <br /> I would say, the &quot;One of My Tribe&quot; ritual does not explicitly give protection from the Beckoning.<br /> The Ritual severs all metaphysical blood ties to their sire, former clan/lineage, and Antediluvian to the point Malkavians are even expelled from the Madness Network<br /> Going with canon again and don't really have much to work with, but severing lineage ties could <i>logically</i> interfere with or weaken such a call similar to how breaking a blood bond or other extreme measures like diablerie/mass vitae consumption can temporarily stave it off in some accounts<br /> <br /> However...<br /> <br /> Even regular Caitiff (without the ritual) can still feel the Beckoning if their Blood Potency is high enough. Panders who undergo the ritual are &quot;clean&quot; of prior lineage, but this isn't cited as a full countermeasure.<br /> <br /> The Beckoning\u200b is a mysterious compulsion drawing higher-generation/lower-Blood Potency vampires - mostly Elders - toward the Middle East and other ancient civilization cradles but again, it isn't explicitly framed as a standard blood bond from one's sire or clan Antediluvian.<br /> We simpyl don't know what is behind it<br /> <br /> But we know who are effected by it - mostly - and no official material added &quot;oh, except the Panders&quot; yet we do have an example of such immunity - the Hecata, so it is not something they left out by accident.<br /> Okay I know I give way too much credit to the V5 writers, but as I said we have to work what we know and that is not that much<br /> So going by assumption? I would say even higher-generation/lower-Blood Potency or Elder Caitiff/Pander were effected<br /> <br /> Just like how the Baali re-Embrace ritual, that similarly cut ties wouldn't protect you or the Gargoyle creation Rite nor the (new) Ahrimane creation rite<br /> Maybe they <i>should </i>IF the Beckoning would be the result of bond or lineage but... we simply do not know<br /> We only know, Vampires <i>are </i>effected if they are old, higher-generation/lower-Blood Potency enough but some managed to delay the effect like Helena, others, younger than her, not<br /> <br /> Frustrating, but without knowing the cause we can't really determine what precents the effect and if you go with RAW? What was published?<br /> Simply it was not highlighted and these and these and these are the exceptions - except the Hecata who are not eve na Clan but more like thrid Sect\u200b formed by Clans who are mostly tied to the Cappadocians who indeed lost their Antediluvian (tho' he &quot;just&quot; became a Wraith, later specter and some of the parts of his soul are still around here and there...) but then there are the Nagaraja who are members but not tied to them yet immune (you could argue, since they used a Settite's blood, the fact Sutekh is MIA since 33. AD could be a factor) but the Samedi and the Pisanob are again wildcards, Drowned legacies? Long lost Cappadocians?<br /> And the Mla Watu a Lineage of the Laibon who are &quot;pure&quot; Cappadocians thchnically, never officially joined and there are no mentions about them being immune...<br /> <br /> You can house rule it, of course<br /> It would be even logical from one point of view, but from another?<br /> Again, without knowing what the Beckoning <b>is </b>and what is behind it?<br /> It is borderline impossible to work out what works or what not and why works what works (eg. Hecata membership of what Helena and other did to deley the effects)<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-17T06:31:06-07:00","id":1560043,"title":"","content":"I doubt it. If the Beckoning is the 3rd generation summoning their lineages to wherever they are. The vauldrie wouldn't be to hard to overcome with their powerful blood as we say what happened to Monty Coven when he consumed Mithras and his Vauldrie was no match for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-17T09:36:25-07:00","id":1560044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1559951-could-the-vaulderie-cure-the-beckoning?p=1560012#post1560012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Frustrating, but without knowing the cause we can't really determine what precents the effect and if you go with RAW? What was published?<br /> Simply it was not highlighted and these and these and these are the exceptions - except the Hecata who are not eve na Clan but more like thrid Sect formed by Clans who are mostly tied to the Cappadocians who indeed lost their Antediluvian (tho' he &quot;just&quot; became a Wraith, later specter and some of the parts of his soul are still around here and there...) but then there are the Nagaraja who are members but not tied to them yet immune (you could argue, since they used a Settite's blood, the fact Sutekh is MIA since 33. AD could be a factor) but the Samedi and the Pisanob are again wildcards, Drowned legacies? Long lost Cappadocians?<br /> And the Mla Watu a Lineage of the Laibon who are &quot;pure&quot; Cappadocians thchnically, never officially joined and there are no mentions about them being immune...<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Giovanni wasn't even a full fledged Antedeluvian anyways.<br /> <br /> He only succeeded in consuming half of Cappadocious' soul, because the plan to diablerize God didn't pan out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-17T16:47:28-07:00","id":1560049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1559951-could-the-vaulderie-cure-the-beckoning?p=1560005#post1560005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, well, if the Vaulderie doesn't break the connection, what about... urgh... the Panders ritual?<br /> <br /> The one that turns you into a Caitiff?<br /> <br /> Can't be compelled by the antedeluvians, if you have no antedeluvian! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>The Beckoning is a plot device, and one that has never been explained (and likely never will be explained).<br /> <br /> There is one theory that the antedeluvians are behind the Beckoning, but that's just a theory. The only clan we know that is immune to the Beckoning is the Cappadocians. Their clan founder happens to be dead so that might be why. But also note that we haven't seen anything saying that Ravnos are immune to the Beckoning and we know that their clan founder is also dead. So there's the possibility that the Beckoning isn't being caused by the Antedeluvians but by something else - maybe the Baali, or surviving Tal'mahe'Ra.<br /> <br /> Gentleman Gamer once noted that the Hecata are immune to the Beckoning because their clan founder as well as most of their Methuselah had been wiped out, but I'm not sure that that ended up becoming official White Wolf canon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 05-17-2026, 07:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-18T00:09:21-07:00","id":1560054,"title":"","content":"Okay, forum ate it - one day I will learn not to edit<br /> <br /> So...<br /> I never really liked that theory to be honest<br /> Mostly because what you wrote before about the Ravnos for example or even the Followers of Set - we don't know what the hell happened with Sutekh, some sources say/suggest he is in the Duat reflection of Ombos, other that he slumbers somewhere<br /> But technically speaking, the Founder is out of the picture like most of the Methuselahs and Ancients<br /> And yet they are still effected<br /> <br /> ..the Hecata/Cappadocians?<br /> <br /> Like Sutekh Sargon/Cappadocius is gone, not really dead, I mean deader than dead, but somewhere in between withs vestiges lingering around in the material world, and other parts in a Wraith then Spectre form in the Underworld, like Sutekh if you go with the Duat theory<br /> And actually more Cappadocian old geezers survived and active than Settite ones, I mean even direct descendants like Byzar, Japeth (as Wraith, but still there) and Lazarus - the trio who are the Capuchin persone, but there are quite a rooster of old ones around, like Angelique, Apacia, Roger de Camden, the Premascine Giovanni (possibly), Lady Constancia (depending of the edition in one form or another) and if you count the Harbringers, Khurshid, the Wearer of the Sun Mask is also old as dirt<br /> The Followers of Set not had many active Hierophants (or that many to begin with) Nakhthorheb, maybe as a tag team with Seterpenre and maybe Maatkare, Neferu, Wepwawet and Sobek if you want to be generous, but some of them are out of order but, even when sleeping like the Sleeping Lord, the Child of the Scorpion King have an AoE that is a heavy disturbance and covers Cairo<br /> Of course we don't know the exact numbers, but I think enough to put a big question mark on that theory<br /> <br /> And we not even mentioned other Clans and Bloodlines (tho' there are not many of those in V5) who are effected yet lack any heavy hitters who could pull such thing off<br /> I mean the Salubri lost almost all of their Methuselahs and Ancients and even Saulot - okay, they got better, Saulot even split in to Hun and P'o version of himself, if you wantto go that way, but at best he is wearing his new Tremere skinsuit, while the old Salubri (again if you don't count the Nkulu Zao or the Wu Zao or the al-Amin) became Tremere breakfast (or got their own Tremere skinsuit as daddy did...) Qawiyya el-Ghaduba and Nahum ben Enosh are possibly still around (Qawiyya I think a confirmed one, ending up on the Red List even?) not to mention Mahtiel or Adonai (who is strongly suspected to be the Dark Ages one, not some pretender)<br /> They are the other end of the spectrum in a sense, the Salbur are effected like anyone else, but not even have the numbers to justify such phenomena or they do have and that is another whole can of worms<br /> <br /> Not to mention the Ravnos, who - okay, if the V5 loresheet about Zapathasura's blood is true, he is not that gone either but most of the elders ended up dead (tho' with that levels of Chimestry? Ask the Kuei-jin how it went to have an all out war with even one elder Ravnos; the best example of whats happened between Harappa a Ravnos stronghold ruled by Chandraputra and Mohenjo-Daro a stronghold of the asuratizayya/the Kuei-Jin was rueld by &quot;Chandraputra's ancent enemy&quot; - The generals on both sides summoned otherworldly powers. They forced \u201cthe light of four suns\u201d to shine at once. The battle turned the river valley red with the blood of thousands of mortals and Kindred. It reportedly lasted a full year and a night, ending with Chandraputra taking the head of his ancient enemy... ) so if anything the Ravnos should be totally immune... yet?<br /> Nope<br /> That few who are still around and have the age, blood potency, generation or just another bad day are effected<br /> <br /> <br /> For that reason I never really bought the \u200bAntedeluvians and/or or powerful Methuselahs are behind the Beckoning, not because the lore not really support that, but because of the inconistencies and the lack of evidance<br /> It IS a good theory, actually as good as any other theory, but we don't know what IS the Beckoning or what causes it, it never it been stated nor explained and as you said, probably it never will be<br /> <br /> And I'm not sure it is better that way...\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 05-18-2026, 04:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-18T01:17:09-07:00","id":1560056,"title":"","content":"The Beckoning could be a plot thread from the Book of Nod. Check around pg 100 ;3","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26219-aydoo","name":"Aydoo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-18T01:37:44-07:00","id":1560057,"title":"","content":"That is the problem<br /> It <b>could</b> be <b><u>many</u> </b>things<br /> I can list at least a dozen things and not even cast my proverbial net that far to touch any crossover material<br /> <br /> Sure this ambiguity gives the ST freedom to tailor the Beckoning to their stories but the problem as I said the irritating and anoying inconsistencies - for example that I wrote about the Antedeluvians and/or or powerful Methuselahs are behind the Beckoning theory<br /> <br /> It is not some trivial thing like Golconda or who killed the Sabbat's Regent Melinda Galbraith Before a Palla Grande in 2001; the theories range wide and far from the Tlacique (unlikely) to the possiblitys he faked her own death on orders from her master Nergal/Huitzilopochtli (highly likely) - tho' this one is another a bit anoying peace - but a global, basically setting (and alegedly non-existent metaplot) defining thing\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 05-18-2026, 04:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-23T05:18:01-07:00","id":1560161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1559951-could-the-vaulderie-cure-the-beckoning?p=1559952#post1559952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think a good test of this logic would be whether the Sabbat Ravnos were less effected by the Week of Nightmares? (I don't think it's mentioned, but I'm actually not sure).</div> </div> </div> </div>As I recall from the revised Clanbook, the Antitribu <i>were</i> affected, although on average more of them survived (outside of all-Ravnos packs, their packmates would often subdue them when they suddenly went psycho on each other, and some packs with only a single Ravnos got dragged along while their packmate thirsted for elder Ravnos blood. In some cases, their packmates <i>didn't even notice a change</i>, which doesn't speak well of their usual unlifestyles).<br /> <br /> So it seems less like the Vinculum was holding them back so much as having non-Ravnos around to restrain/beat some sense into them. Any Ravnos of strong enough blood to get Beckoned (<i>are</i> there any left?) are probably not getting stopped the same way by their elder peers, since they're <i>also</i> in the same boat, possibly literally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2218-ideon","name":"Ideon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-25T07:36:46-07:00","id":1560208,"title":"","content":"Well, there's also the fact that Ravnos was originally presented as being a 2nd generation (which would mean all of his direct childer would be able to throw down with Antedeluvians.), and he has access to the highest levels of Chimerstry. Which generates illusions of such convincing realism, that you're effectively an Awakened Mage.<br /> <br /> If Ravnos wanted to fake his death by putting the world in a mass delusion, he certainly has the power to do so.<br /> <br /> Also, this would theoretically make Ravnos the most powerful of the 13 clans. Since A) their generations are 1 step lower than everybody else, and B) they fuck with Consensus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":29027,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","user":"GreatHornedRatkin","date":". 05-25-2026, 10:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-25T08:40:49-07:00","id":1560210,"title":"","content":"Almost<br /> I mean if you with that story, Ravnos was embraced by Caine (whom they call Kaen) and he embraced Ennoia and presumbaly, others, like Churka for example or Zapathasura (that could be Churka's alternate name) but he ended up nailed to the roof to greet the Sun<br /> The Ravnos would be still normal clan ,decended from Churka or Zapathasura (who in this story is not made by the gods, just made up the story to justify their presence in Middle Kingdom and war against the Kuei Jin)<br /> Same if they decended from Dracian who Irad Embraced to spy on the others of the 3rd gen and then wandered to east","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-29T14:01:50-07:00","id":1561108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1559951-could-the-vaulderie-cure-the-beckoning?p=1560208#post1560208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, this would theoretically make Ravnos the most powerful of the 13 clans. Since A) their generations are 1 step lower than everybody else, and B) they fuck with Consensus.</div> </div> </div> </div>All clans are descendants from the 2nd Generation, that's kind of what Generation means. And their power level is literally known and just the same as everyone else. This made no sense.<br /> <br /> Did anyone ever said where exactly in the Middle East the affected by the Beckoning were going to?<br /> <br /> Because that's about as helpful a description as saying &quot;called to North America&quot;. It's not a strange empty land few people ever braved, it's a very populous modern place just as any other","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-30T02:54:19-07:00","id":1561122,"title":"","content":"The Sabbat were said to have fought the Gehenna War under the cover of the Afghanistan and Iraqi wars, so those two places are likely included. But I'd also add in the Levant and Iran, and probably a few other places around there.<br /> <br /> Per the <i>Book of Nod</i>, p. 100:<br /> <br /> &quot;On the second day, Caine will return And call his Children to the meeting place<br /> on the site of the First City he will beckon<br /> them, sitting on his basalt throne.&quot;<br /> <br /> He goes on to judge those who are unworthy (including diablerists), and then kills them. This seems ironic, given that diablerie appears to delay the Beckoning. So maybe the elders aren't running to Caine, but to his grandchilder? (Page 99 says they will eat everyone.) Maybe those who stay behind will actually be the ones getting judged?<br /> <br /> My understanding is that those who are immune to the Beckoning are so because they have no Antediluvian. There have always been hints that an Antediluvian has the power to call/summon/affect their entire clan, even if some of them seem able to resist. So this seems to be a &quot;sympathy of the blood&quot; thing\u2014just as Tremere was able to call the Tremere <i>antitribu</i> to him (per <i>Nights of Prophecy</i>) and Ravnos' descendants went mad when he apparently died.<br /> <br /> The Feast of Folly might be an older example. The Family Reunion itself may have been something similar (but perhaps weaker, since it was only Fourth Generation elders responsible), and that may be the real reason everyone turned up and played nice. It also required the Old Man in the Mountain to agree to the Treaty of Tyre to curse his entire clan. And the Malkavian Methuselahs behind the Great Prank may have been doing something similar, too.<br /> <br /> <b>tl;dr: </b>It works through blood sympathy. The eldest can draw their descendants to them, or even affect them at large given enough oomph to do so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":".  Clarify 06-30-2026, 05:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-30T05:27:08-07:00","id":1561127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1559951-could-the-vaulderie-cure-the-beckoning?p=1561122#post1561122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sabbat were said to have fought the Gehenna War under the cover of the Afghanistan and Iraqi wars, so those two places are likely included. But I'd also add in the Levant and Iran, and probably a few other places around there.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe, but those are not only widely apart places, but still huge areas.<br /> <br /> The problem remains exactly the same: it talks about the Gehenna War as happening in a distant land near something relevant, but it actually covers a continent-size area in a very active part of the world that's well known (and home to some players) and doesn't really give any meaningful goal once you arrive.<br /> <br /> Where are they heading?<br /> What are the victims of the Beckoning doing?<br /> What the Sabbat is actually engaging?<br /> What the locals, including local Kindred, have to say?<br /> <br /> I won't rest with an answer that keeps treating anything outside the G7 countries as exotic tokenism, I want something that's both actually respectful with the place and useful to run games there. I'm not against making it as fan material, but wished we had any improvement at this point.<br /> <br /> For now it's still exactly as if all the by Night books were in European cities, and then for this war they said the Beckoning is moving elders to North America, then just never touch the matter again as if no one lived in North America. Saying they used as covers events in opposite sides of Canada doesn't do much.<br /> <br /> As for the source of the Beckoning, it isn't all that strange that those to be punished get to resist going to be punished. But I don't think the Antes are the best option.<br /> <br /> Not only we have the problems Shadeprowler pointed: no other clan or faction has shown particular resistance, neither do Caitiff and Panders, only the Hecata.<br /> <br /> But also I just find it too clich\u00e9 with no payback for the narrative. Especially if you think the Antes may not be all in the same place, sharing the same plan.<br /> <br /> For me the Beckoning reads more like the kind of pervasive effect, neither forceful or precise, but ever present, that's either a passive result of something happening/someone's presence, or some kind of natural law itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-01T05:21:38-07:00","id":1561156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1559951-could-the-vaulderie-cure-the-beckoning?p=1561108#post1561108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> All clans are descendants from the 2nd Generation, that's kind of what Generation means. And their power level is literally known and just the same as everyone else. This made no sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, all clans are descended from the 3rd generation. If Ravnos was originally presented as being a 2nd generation vampire, then that means he should theoretically be the second most powerful vampire on the planet, next to Caine himself.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1559951-could-the-vaulderie-cure-the-beckoning?p=1561108#post1561108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Did anyone ever said where exactly in the Middle East the affected by the Beckoning were going to?<br /> <br /> Because that's about as helpful a description as saying &quot;called to North America&quot;. It's not a strange empty land few people ever braved, it's a very populous modern place just as any other</div> </div> </div> </div>Context clues can pretty much tell us what part of the middle east they were referring to.<br /> <br /> Sabbat are stated to have joined up with mortal terrorist organizations, so it's not hard to connect the dots there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-01T07:01:38-07:00","id":1561159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1559951-could-the-vaulderie-cure-the-beckoning?p=1561156#post1561156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, all clans are descended from the 3rd generation. If Ravnos was originally presented as being a 2nd generation vampire, then that means he should theoretically be the second most powerful vampire on the planet, next to Caine himself.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're no less a descendant from your grandparents just because you're a descendant from your parents.<br /> <br /> If we assume Noddism as true, and so the 3rd Gen is exactly what it says on the tin, then they are descendants from the 2nd Gen. This is basic genealogy.<br /> <br /> For the clans to not be descendants from the 2nd Gen they would have to come from an Ante that spontaneously appeared already as 3rd Gen.<br /> <br /> Also, a 13th Gen Ravnos is a 13th Gen Kindred. The Generations are not counted from distance to the Ante (that's usually impossible to determine), but from Caine, and verified by the power they manifest.<br /> <br /> On top of we having rules for Ravnos and they are perfectly normal in this regard.<br /> <br /> There's zero room in the canon for the clan to secretly be 1 Gen lower than the rest across the board. It simply makes no sense in the official setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1559951-could-the-vaulderie-cure-the-beckoning?p=1561156#post1561156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Context clues can pretty much tell us what part of the middle east they were referring to.<br /> <br /> Sabbat are stated to have joined up with mortal terrorist organizations, so it's not hard to connect the dots there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then by all means, please enlighten me on what part it is, then.<br /> <br /> On my part, having been both studying and accompanying for the last 30 years the activities of organizations like Al-Qaeda, Fatah, Hezbollah, Hamas, Taleban and Islamic State, the list of orgs generally lumped together as terrorists despite that being incorrect for most, I am utterly clueless about where the heck in the Middle East the Gehenna War is happening.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-01T07:18:47-07:00","id":1561160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1559951-could-the-vaulderie-cure-the-beckoning?p=1561159#post1561159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're no less a descendant from your grandparents just because you're a descendant from your parents.<br /> <br /> If we assume Noddism as true, and so the 3rd Gen is exactly what it says on the tin, then they are descendants from the 2nd Gen. This is basic genealogy.<br /> <br /> For the clans to not be descendants from the 2nd Gen they would have to come from an Ante that spontaneously appeared already as 3rd Gen.<br /> <br /> Also, a 13th Gen Ravnos is a 13th Gen Kindred. The Generations are not counted from distance to the Ante (that's usually impossible to determine), but from Caine, and verified by the power they manifest.<br /> <br /> On top of we having rules for Ravnos and they are perfectly normal in this regard.<br /> <br /> There's zero room in the canon for the clan to secretly be 1 Gen lower than the rest across the board. It simply makes no sense in the official setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think you're getting the point?<br /> <br /> Each subsequent generation of vampire is weaker than the one that came before.<br /> <br /> 2nd gen is weaker than 1st, while 3rd gen is weaker than 2nd, est.<br /> <br /> The Antedeluvians are two steps removed from Caine, while the 2nd generation is only 1 step.<br /> <br /> As a member of the 2nd generation, all of Ravnos' direct childer would be members of the 3rd generation, who would then go on to sire 4th gens. Thus, all members of clan Ravnos would be 1 generation lower, depending on how far back you trace their ancestry.<br /> <br /> <br /> Followers of Set, on the other hand, consider their antedeluvian to be a true 1st generation, and thus claim that all of their respective members are 2 steps lower. A 9th generation Setite, for example, would be considered 7th generation within the clan social structure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-01T09:27:37-07:00","id":1561163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1559951-could-the-vaulderie-cure-the-beckoning?p=1561160#post1561160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think you're getting the point?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I did. Half of my answer addresses this directly.<br /> <br /> No one calls a given Ravnos, or anyone else, a 13\u00ba Gen because they counted every sire until the Ante.<br /> <br /> They call it because the vampire exhibits the powers of the 13\u00ba Gen, and detection magic says they're 13\u00ba Gen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-01T10:31:38-07:00","id":1561165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1559951-could-the-vaulderie-cure-the-beckoning?p=1561163#post1561163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I did. Half of my answer addresses this directly.<br /> <br /> No one calls a given Ravnos, or anyone else, a 13\u00ba Gen because they counted every sire until the Ante.<br /> <br /> They call it because the vampire exhibits the powers of the 13\u00ba Gen, and detection magic says they're 13\u00ba Gen.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm almost positive the Ventrue would strongly disagree with that claim. Seeing as they take matters of lineage very seriously, and train their childer to memorize and recite their ancestry as far back as possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-01T11:20:07-07:00","id":1561166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1559951-could-the-vaulderie-cure-the-beckoning?p=1561165#post1561165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm almost positive the Ventrue would strongly disagree with that claim. Seeing as they take matters of lineage very seriously, and train their childer to memorize and recite their ancestry as far back as possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>They won't because diablerie: when you reduce Generation that way, you are counted by your new power level, not your original lineage. That means even the Ventrue will consider power before sire counting.<br /> <br /> Also, they have gaps, many. Tradition dictates you go as far back as possible, but Ante isn't usually possible. They have a whole game of humiliation among themselves by disproving each other's lineages if given the opportunity, so at the same time that an impressive lineage is a big asset, having a tight claim is worth more than going all the way back.<br /> <br /> Remember they can't even agree on the names of their 4th Generation beyond Mithras, or if Mithras' sire was indeed [Ventrue] or a diablerist.<br /> <br /> Now, one thing is certain: the Ventrue will no doubt keep record of all suspect or confirmed diablerie just to keep lineages straight, noting Original Generation vs Current Generation vs Distance from oldest verifiable ancestor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-01T23:22:25-07:00","id":1561186,"title":"","content":"In our game, we are treating the Beckoning as the 3rd generation wherever they may dwell calling upon some of the older and powerful members of their clans for judgement. Some will come back notably weaker or stronger or not at all but in the end not much else is known yet. Others are not called at all despite their age and power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-02T04:50:53-07:00","id":1561188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1559951-could-the-vaulderie-cure-the-beckoning?p=1561186#post1561186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In our game, we are treating the Beckoning as the 3rd generation wherever they may dwell calling upon some of the older and powerful members of their clans for judgement. Some will come back notably weaker or stronger or not at all but in the end not much else is known yet. Others are not called at all despite their age and power.</div> </div> </div> </div>In mine the 3rd Generation itself is trying to find out what is happening. The Beckoning is seemingly random and comes and goes, can attract the victim wherever and their behavior is erratic when they arrive. Until it suddenly isn't anymore.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind that in my lore the Gehenna isn't really a thing, and most Antes were active this whole time anyway. I'm even working on loresheets to represent contact with them and how it marks you.<br /> <br /> But they're not behind the Beckoning and are puzzled, even afraid: more powerful vampires seem just even more vulnerable when they're affected. One wonders what would happen if one of the Antes were Beckoned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-02T11:26:44-07:00","id":1561194,"title":"","content":"That sounds interesting Montparnasse about having the 3rd generation being more active in your games. Do you have any problems with power imbalances using them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 07-02-2026, 10:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-02T17:28:49-07:00","id":1561210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1559951-could-the-vaulderie-cure-the-beckoning?p=1561194#post1561194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sounds interesting Montparnasse about having the 3rd generation being more active in your games<br /> games. Do you have any problems with power imbalances using them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope.<br /> <br /> I use as principle that with time most vampires notice their powers are blunt instruments, and careful application of lesser ones or just skill is more useful in the long run, and a more worthy challenge.<br /> <br /> Also that the Antes have less grandiose goals most of the time, because at the level of power they're in, their usual interests are either utterly mundane, alien, or both, while the big ones require too careful action for displays of power to be worth it.<br /> <br /> Think Saulot in <i>Lair of the Hidden</i> working as a humble servant, because the low profile while simply being there is way more effective to get what he wants.<br /> <br /> Overall the secret to have high power NPCs in game without breaking everything is to have them under constraints: abusing power is easy, but won't get what you really want. Also never let any explanation of what they want land as a trustworthy conclusion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-02T18:00:34-07:00","id":1561211,"title":"","content":"Vampires don't want to be challenged. That's why the elders stay in their castles all the time, making the neonates do all the hard work for them. And why they backstab each other when it looks like somebody is starting to accrue too much power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-02T20:12:29-07:00","id":1561214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1559951-could-the-vaulderie-cure-the-beckoning?p=1561211#post1561211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires don't want to be challenged. That's why the elders stay in their castles all the time, making the neonates do all the hard work for them. And why they backstab each other when it looks like somebody is starting to accrue too much power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except when they do because they're also passionate beings that put a stern face but do a lot of things out of whims, and conspire most of the time to stave off the boredom of eternity, both recurring themes in the books and many official characters.<br /> <br /> Any simplification into a single behavior profile misses the actual tension and variability in the undead, and the available material objectively demonstrates this.<br /> <br /> Not to say that those are the Antes, they're not bound to 'normal' Vampire behavior, or even to their own previous behavior from more than a thousand years ago.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-02T20:57:52-07:00","id":1561216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1559951-could-the-vaulderie-cure-the-beckoning?p=1561214#post1561214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except when they do because they're also passionate beings that put a stern face but do a lot of things out of whims, and conspire most of the time to stave off the boredom of eternity, both recurring themes in the books and many official characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Passion was the signature trait of clan Brujah. If everybody is passionate, then the Rabble have nothing to distinguish themselves from the other clans. They're just a bunch of ass holes, that fire bomb people they disagree with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-03T02:24:54-07:00","id":1561221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1559951-could-the-vaulderie-cure-the-beckoning?p=1561216#post1561216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Passion was the signature trait of clan Brujah. If everybody is passionate, then the Rabble have nothing to distinguish themselves from the other clans. They're just a bunch of ass holes, that fire bomb people they disagree with.</div> </div> </div> </div>The books literally state repeatedly in the main blurb that vampires are passionate across the board, and several official characters of every clan show this.<br /> <br /> Passions can take many forms. What makes the Brujah distinct is intensity and direction: they're ideological. Their passion is about how society should work, about politics and ethics.<br /> <br /> And their curse is about loss of control to anger, a specific kind of passion. There is no conflict between Kindred being passionate and the Brujah having their own brand of passion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-04T11:10:40-07:00","id":1561303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1559951-could-the-vaulderie-cure-the-beckoning?p=1560208#post1560208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, there's also the fact that Ravnos was originally presented as being a 2nd generation (which would mean all of his direct childer would be able to throw down with Antedeluvians.), and he has access to the highest levels of Chimerstry. Which generates illusions of such convincing realism, that you're effectively an Awakened Mage.<br /> <br /> If Ravnos wanted to fake his death by putting the world in a mass delusion, he certainly has the power to do so.<br /> <br /> Also, this would theoretically make Ravnos the most powerful of the 13 clans. Since A) their generations are 1 step lower than everybody else, and B) they fuck with Consensus.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure that that checks out. At the 3rd Generation, vampires can access 10th level Disciplines, Plot Devices, the maximal power of any given Discipline. So if 3rd is actually weaker than 2nd, there would have to be something beyond Plot Device (insert Gurren Lagann joke here). <br /> <br /> According to the <i>Erciyes Fragments</i>, the weakening of the Blood started at the creation of the Clans, which makes sense connecting to this paradigm. In this recounting, Caine maintained his status as the vampire king because of the One Above's Mark, which he seemingly exagerrated the strength of.<br /> <br /> So, the unique power of a 2nd generation vampire would be to create 3rd generation vampires, not to have some sort of 11th level Discipline or other such nonsense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26432-jagnestormskull","name":"JagneStormskull","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26432_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-05T04:35:32-07:00","id":1561342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JagneStormskull</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1559951-could-the-vaulderie-cure-the-beckoning?p=1561303#post1561303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure that that checks out. At the 3rd Generation, vampires can access 10th level Disciplines, Plot Devices, the maximal power of any given Discipline. So if 3rd is actually weaker than 2nd, there would have to be something beyond Plot Device (insert Gurren Lagann joke here).<br /> <br /> According to the <i>Erciyes Fragments</i>, the weakening of the Blood started at the creation of the Clans, which makes sense connecting to this paradigm. In this recounting, Caine maintained his status as the vampire king because of the One Above's Mark, which he seemingly exagerrated the strength of.<br /> <br /> So, the unique power of a 2nd generation vampire would be to create 3rd generation vampires, not to have some sort of 11th level Discipline or other such nonsense.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't really need an 11 dot version of Chimerstry, when the 10th dot is powerful enough to make your illusions function as though they were real.<br /> <br /> You're effectively playing an Awakened Mage at that point.<br /> <br /> <br /> No, what makes him more powerful, would be the increased blood potency, and his ability to exert greater levels of power in one turn than his 3rd generation counterparts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-05T07:45:24-07:00","id":1561343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1559951-could-the-vaulderie-cure-the-beckoning?p=1561127#post1561127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe, but those are not only widely apart places, but still huge areas.<br /> <br /> The problem remains exactly the same: it talks about the Gehenna War as happening in a distant land near something relevant, but it actually covers a continent-size area in a very active part of the world that's well known (and home to some players) and doesn't really give any meaningful goal once you arrive.<br /> <br /> Where are they heading?<br /> What are the victims of the Beckoning doing?<br /> What the Sabbat is actually engaging?<br /> What the locals, including local Kindred, have to say?<br /> <br /> I won't rest with an answer that keeps treating anything outside the G7 countries as exotic tokenism, I want something that's both actually respectful with the place and useful to run games there. I'm not against making it as fan material, but wished we had any improvement at this point.<br /> <br /> For now it's still exactly as if all the by Night books were in European cities, and then for this war they said the Beckoning is moving elders to North America, then just never touch the matter again as if no one lived in North America. Saying they used as covers events in opposite sides of Canada doesn't do much.<br /> <br /> As for the source of the Beckoning, it isn't all that strange that those to be punished get to resist going to be punished. But I don't think the Antes are the best option.<br /> <br /> Not only we have the problems Shadeprowler pointed: no other clan or faction has shown particular resistance, neither do Caitiff and Panders, only the Hecata.<br /> <br /> But also I just find it too clich\u00e9 with no payback for the narrative. Especially if you think the Antes may not be all in the same place, sharing the same plan.<br /> <br /> For me the Beckoning reads more like the kind of pervasive effect, neither forceful or precise, but ever present, that's either a passive result of something happening/someone's presence, or some kind of natural law itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the record, I agree with you that it's vague and stupid and offensive. But also, I don't think you'll find a canon answer that you like any better. At least, not in V5. V6 may fix this for us.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-05T10:17:08-07:00","id":1561347,"title":"","content":"I don't think V6 will fix it Adambeyoncelowe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-05T11:40:33-07:00","id":1561349,"title":"","content":"Kinded do like conflict DarkKing no matter how old they are as it helps to keep themselves for falling to beast and pass the time.<br /> <br /> Hesha and Beckett are passionate about learning the origins of their kind and if it riles up older and powerful beings. So much the better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-05T16:59:36-07:00","id":1561358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1559951-could-the-vaulderie-cure-the-beckoning?p=1561342#post1561342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, what makes him more powerful, would be the increased blood potency, and his ability to exert greater levels of power in one turn than his 3rd generation counterparts.</div> </div> </div> </div>And where's the table that confirms that?<br /> <br /> Because without rules, we have no reason to think this difference existed. If the thinning of the blood started with the 4th Generation, that means exactly that there would be no distinct Blood Potency/Generation Table for the 2nd.<br /> <br /> It would be irrelevant anyway. There's still a 3rd Generation following, and the clan descends from them like everyone else. No one ever used the actual counting of sires to determine the &quot;power of the Generation&quot; of anyone.<br /> <br /> Keeping in mind that previous editions have no Blood Potency to talk about, it's Generation doing all the work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1559951-could-the-vaulderie-cure-the-beckoning?p=1561343#post1561343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For the record, I agree with you that it's vague and stupid and offensive. But also, I don't think you'll find a canon answer that you like any better. At least, not in V5. V6 may fix this for us.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not betting on it, but I hope so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-05T17:22:49-07:00","id":1561363,"title":"","content":"It was always blood pool and how high it was depending on the generation of the kindred. Blood potency was a more recent addition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-06T11:54:21-07:00","id":1561394,"title":"","content":"The fact they're going back to basics and trying out all the old editions suggests to me they're open to changing things if needed. It's just not clear whether we'll like those changes.<br /> <br /> But on re-reading a bunch of my old books recently, I was taken back by how much I loved some of the material. Like, The Chalice of Osseous Delights in Clanbook: Tzimisce Revised? Amazing! I loved them so much, I had to add the pack to the WWWiki\u2014and then ended up adding every single pack member after that. <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/The_Chalice_of_Osseous_Delights\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Th...seous_Delights</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-08T23:29:39-07:00","id":1561504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1559951-could-the-vaulderie-cure-the-beckoning?p=1561358#post1561358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And where's the table that confirms that?<br /> <br /> Because without rules, we have no reason to think this difference existed. If the thinning of the blood started with the 4th Generation, that means exactly that there would be no distinct Blood Potency/Generation Table for the 2nd.<br /> <br /> It would be irrelevant anyway. There's still a 3rd Generation following, and the clan descends from them like everyone else. No one ever used the actual counting of sires to determine the &quot;power of the Generation&quot; of anyone.<br /> <br /> Keeping in mind that previous editions have no Blood Potency to talk about, it's Generation doing all the work.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Not betting on it, but I hope so.</div> </div> </div> </div>The curse of generations didn't exist before the 2nd were wiped out, but it did afterward. <br /> <br /> And we know the curse did not just start at 3rd and begin working its way down, because that would imply that the 3rd generation would be only 1 step removed from Caine on the power scale.<br /> <br /> If they hate him and wanted to destroy him, they could have done so. There was 1 Caine, and at least 13 Antedeluvians (possibly more, depending on which Gehenna scenario we follow). I'm pretty sure they had the advantage there.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, we kind of do have rules, when Caine's character sheet just keeps spamming <i>&quot;Caine Wins&quot;</i> in every category.<br /> <br /> That would be strange if Caine was operating on the same power scale system as everyone else. But instead, it sounds more like he has access to a level of abilities even the Antedeluvians can't replicate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-09T00:23:13-07:00","id":1561506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1559951-could-the-vaulderie-cure-the-beckoning?p=1561504#post1561504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The curse of generations didn't exist before the 2nd were wiped out, but it did afterward.<br /> <br /> And we know the curse did not just start at 3rd and begin working its way down, because that would imply that the 3rd generation would be only 1 step removed from Caine on the power scale.<br /> <br /> If they hate him and wanted to destroy him, they could have done so. There was 1 Caine, and at least 13 Antedeluvians (possibly more, depending on which Gehenna scenario we follow). I'm pretty sure they had the advantage there.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, we kind of do have rules, when Caine's character sheet just keeps spamming <i>&quot;Caine Wins&quot;</i> in every category.<br /> <br /> That would be strange if Caine was operating on the same power scale system as everyone else. But instead, it sounds more like he has access to a level of abilities even the Antedeluvians can't replicate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Caine is unique because he was cursed directly by God. In <i>Gehenna</i>, they say that anyone who harms Caine suffers the same fate seven times over. Even if that's not true, his childer and grandchildren may have believed it was so, and that would explain why they never bothered ganking him.<br /> <br /> Also, Caine never had to be Embraced. For all we know, he never even died either. His curse may have just been layered on top of a living primordial being. And the early humans of the Bible seem to live for a really long time anyway, which implies they're not quite the same as the people who came later.<br /> <br /> And maybe, as the First Vampire, it's like Akasha. Maybe if you kill him, the whole of vampirekind perishes. That's not to mention that he probably mastered every Discipline at 10 before his childer were ever created, so he has a broader set of skills than they ever could.<br /> <br /> There's enough special snowflake-ism there that it makes sense there are other factors elevating him above his childer\u2014or making it so they can't kill them\u2014without it necessarily being due to a weakening of the Blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-09T08:12:36-07:00","id":1561520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1559951-could-the-vaulderie-cure-the-beckoning?p=1561504#post1561504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Caine</div> </div> </div> </div>Cursed by YHWH<br /> Protected by The Mark of Cain<br /> Cursed/Empowered by Angels<br /> Trained by the Crone/Lilith/Both<br /> <u><b><i>Arguably</i></b></u> a Vampire<br /> <br /> Let's assume Noddism is true: still Caine is not just 1st Generation, he's Caine. He may not be a Kindred at all to begin with but a cursed thing that generates Vampires.<br /> <br /> By the way, may be still generating Vampires.<br /> <br /> Add to this: new Vampires of any Generation start game with the same dots of any Children of the Night. By all accounts, each Ante could have impressive 3 or 4 in their signature Discipline at the time, we'd be none the wiser and they would certainly need numbers to take out the 2nd Generation and be powerless against Caine without any difference in Blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-09T16:32:12-07:00","id":1561536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1559951-could-the-vaulderie-cure-the-beckoning?p=1561520#post1561520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Cursed by YHWH<br /> Protected by The Mark of Cain<br /> Cursed/Empowered by Angels<br /> Trained by the Crone/Lilith/Both<br /> <u><b><i>Arguably</i></b></u> a Vampire<br /> <br /> Let's assume Noddism is true: still Caine is not just 1st Generation, he's Caine. He may not be a Kindred at all to begin with but a cursed thing that generates Vampires.<br /> <br /> By the way, may be still generating Vampires.<br /> <br /> Add to this: new Vampires of any Generation start game with the same dots of any Children of the Night. By all accounts, each Ante could have impressive 3 or 4 in their signature Discipline at the time, we'd be none the wiser and they would certainly need numbers to take out the 2nd Generation and be powerless against Caine without any difference in Blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>Caine was cursed by first Adam, then himself (Awakened theory) or the Umbrood/Angels. God never has anything to do with him. It was one of the biggest sticking points in his history as God has turned his face from him, starting with his sacrifice.<br /> <br /> The curse of weakening comes from Caine himself, after the flood, when he curses the clan heads with their signature weaknesses. Its the final curse and the herald of his return when the blood is no more potent than normal man. (Ercyes Fragments)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26219-aydoo","name":"Aydoo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-09T16:34:39-07:00","id":1561538,"title":"","content":"The Ercyes Fragments is my favorite lore book and I personally think closet to the truth of the origins of the Kindred.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-09T18:44:24-07:00","id":1561543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aydoo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1559951-could-the-vaulderie-cure-the-beckoning?p=1561536#post1561536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Ercyes Fragments)</div> </div> </div> </div>Not actual canon. It's a specific text. The books are beyond clear that no particular Nod fragment is trustworthy.<br /> <br /> Common Kindred lore states that YHWH did it, period. Unless there's a reason to assume Ercyes as true, it's irrelevant.<br /> <br /> And wouldn't change things much anyway, he's still a unique being rather than a common Kindred.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-09T19:05:26-07:00","id":1561545,"title":"","content":"Even in the Fragments, the Kindred author's make it clear that the Mark of Caine is a major advantage in a war of ageless beings. Though some wonder if Liath could kill Caine and not set off the curse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-11T02:15:54-07:00","id":1561596,"title":"","content":"To add to what others have said, there's a big thing in-setting about the Curse of Caine being divine and therefore not breakable by ordinary means (IIRC, <i>ST Handbook Revised</i> says you need to score more successes than God to break the curse). This is reinforced by <i>The Red Sign</i>.<br /> <br /> There's a suggestion in one of the <i>Gehenna</i> scenarios that Caine may have cursed himself, but there's also the fact any harm visited on Caine is dealt seven times over to anyone else (which is not a curse any of the texts attribute to angels). So even if we assume the curses of sunlight, sustenance, and fire are angelic rather than purely divine, the original Mark of Caine is still supposed to be from God.<br /> <br /> Though, I generally like the suggestion that the weakening of the blood only occurred after the Third Generation. But for the reasons already stated, that doesn't mean the Second and Third Generations are at all equal to Caine in accomplishment\u2014only in potential. The fact remains that he has had longer at this than anyone else (Lilith possibly excepted, but she's her own breed).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-11T07:23:09-07:00","id":1561604,"title":"","content":"Idea for a chronicle:<br /> <br /> The PCs are all recently Embraced. Normal creation rules for Neonates/CotN, normal limit on each Trait, but can't buy anything related to sire or Generation.<br /> <br /> ST can toy around with in-clans and Weakness. Each PC may be unique, mix clans, or just be normal, don't matter. Also keep Generation, BP secret from them, let them find out as they play<br /> <br /> Give them the traits of the 3rd Gen (in V5 initial BP 6 or 7 will do). They don't know, but they're 2nd Gen. Can do as they please, but hiding it is probably safer since they're still low stats CotN<br /> <br /> After a few sessions, Elders from distant cities start to appear. They seek the PCs directly, as if they know exactly where they are. They do. You decide if they're hostile, curious, sycophantic or just weird.<br /> <br /> Congrats: the PCs <i>are</i> the <u><b>Beckoning</b></u>. If they go seek for answers, there are others like them all over the world, though it started somewhere in the Middle East. Maybe others have answers or maybe the trail shows the path of their secret sire, and some points in it may reveal whatever you want.<br /> <br /> Don't worry if they go after anything else, just enjoy toying with the Beckoning as a constant source of weirdness in their lives. The only loss is that they may never know shit about their sire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-12T11:33:14-07:00","id":1561629,"title":"","content":"It's a little notion I like to toy around with sometimes: exactly zero reasons exist for any older vampire/proto-vampire to not Embrace new Childe. The idea that lower Gen are only old vamps is kinda bonkers.<br /> <br /> Wanna use some low Gen in your Chronicle without involving them directly? Just drop new Childer from them, they're not powerful and let it transpire that those older monsters are still about and kicking.<br /> <br /> A 4th Gen Childe is already a huger sign of the Antes wandering around than any Thin Blood will ever be.<br /> <br /> Other idea to toy with: the game is full of scattered signs that the &quot;Thin Blood Phenomenon&quot; always existed, and as time passes the bar of where it happens dynamically changes.<br /> <br /> Use it. Have once or twice an Elder that's secretly Thin Blood while being lower Gen, a remnant of another age. In V5 you can do that by adding T-B traits to someone with higher BP.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-12T11:43:09-07:00","id":1561631,"title":"","content":"There's no real reason for a young 4th-6th generation neonate can't be running around and certainly would cause big concerns for the visible movers and shakers of Kindred society as what kind of role is he or she serving for a ancient sire.<br /> <br /> I'm our game the 4th-6th generation are the more shadowy manipulators of there society with the 3rd generation being only concerned with their personal interests and culling the unworthy from the clans via the Beckoning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-12T12:35:22-07:00","id":1561634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1559951-could-the-vaulderie-cure-the-beckoning?p=1561631#post1561631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no real reason for a young 4th-6th generation neonate can't be running around and certainly would cause big concerns for the visible movers and shakers of Kindred society as what kind of role is he or she serving for a ancient sire.<br /> <br /> I'm our game the 4th-6th generation are the more shadowy manipulators of there society with the 3rd generation being only concerned with their personal interests and culling the unworthy from the clans via the Beckoning.</div> </div> </div> </div>I strictly run it by age to drive the point.<br /> <br /> Younger low Gen exist. Older high Gen also exist. Both are rare due to attrition, but they're there.<br /> <br /> Most young low Gen that survive keep a low profile. They learn soon that letting their Gen transpire will make them targets way before they can defend themselves. They're likely to keep this for as long as they're significantly less powerful than older higher Gen.<br /> <br /> Old high Gen are likely to not have survived to this day as they're the most affected by regular attrition rates and Thin Blood persecution of their time (with or without TB rules, a 13th Gen hundreds of years ago would have been seen as a Thin Blood). If they do, they're likely to both have committed Diablerie and/or lie their Generation successfully, maybe through items and tricks to pretend greater powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-14T05:40:37-07:00","id":1561676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1559951-could-the-vaulderie-cure-the-beckoning?p=1561629#post1561629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Other idea to toy with: the game is full of scattered signs that the &quot;Thin Blood Phenomenon&quot; always existed, and as time passes the bar of where it happens dynamically changes.<br /> <br /> Use it. Have once or twice an Elder that's secretly Thin Blood while being lower Gen, a remnant of another age. In V5 you can do that by adding T-B traits to someone with higher BP.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mmm, no. The only way that would work is if A) they're from a lineage who ran around embracing anybody they could get their hands on. Or B), they are a survivor of one of the previous Gehenna cycles.<br /> <br /> <br /> All Thinbloods are Caitiff (in 5th edition), but not all Caitiff are Thinbloods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-14T06:38:40-07:00","id":1561679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1559951-could-the-vaulderie-cure-the-beckoning?p=1561676#post1561676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mmm, no. The only way that would work is if A) they're from a lineage who ran around embracing anybody they could get their hands on. Or B), they are a survivor of one of the previous Gehenna cycles.<br /> <br /> <br /> All Thinbloods are Caitiff (in 5th edition), but not all Caitiff are Thinbloods.</div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC you can have the Thin Blood Flaw at 13\u00ba Gen in Dark Ages.<br /> <br /> The books aren't definitive about how this worked in the past, only how it works now. The Kindred society is said to always have lived under the impression they're seeing the Time of Thin Blood, interpreting the highest common Generation of the time as the highest possible.<br /> <br /> Several times it was implied that effects of the thinning of Blood may not be linked to specific Generations, but instead move as time goes on. So once upon a time the 6th Generation could not Embrace, had higher frequency of the Caitiff, and exhibited strange properties. Then it moved to the 7th, then 8th. By DA it was the 13th, and in the 90s was the 14th. Now is 16th.<br /> <br /> Also, this would explain the history of when the Generations appear, because seriously, it's not credible that no one at each Generation could Embrace after at most 5 to 10 decades. Even if sires were stricter, it would be just a matter of years for a childe to screw up and hide, or even a sire just cede.<br /> <br /> With at least 5k years of history, I'd expect the vampire society to be at least seeing the 50th Generation, not the 15th. The 13th should have appeared 3500 years ago at worst.<br /> <br /> By the way, even in 5th Ed Thin Bloods can have the signs of their clan. But I'm not talking Caitiff, I'm saying someone who wants can run a Thin Blood Methuselah of 7th Generation and the canon isn't really broken by this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}